{
  "dom_id": "questionExplanation-117652",
  "name": null,
  "problem": "",
  "worked_solution": "The solid is a **rectangular pyramid** since it has a rectangular base and the other $4$ triangular faces meet at a single point.   \n\nAlso, notice that:\n\n- The solid is not a cube since not all of its faces are squares.\n\n- The solid is not a triangular prism because it does not have two triangular bases connected by parallel line segments.\n\n- The solid is not a triangular pyramid since its base is not triangular.\n\n- The solid is not a heptagonal pyramid since its base is not a heptagon.",
